  "behavior": [
    "A module worker loads, hashes and validates the catalog and every book against the current release, then builds an in-memory normalized index. The UI receives bounded result pages with untouched source snippets; no entire text collection is copied from the UI to the worker.",
    "Query matching retains existing phrase, reference, case, Unicode and paragraph-boundary behavior. Original text and printed-supplement origin labels remain unchanged. The last complete match set is reused for pagination.",
    "Requests are tied to protocol, release, source hash and monotonically increasing IDs. New queries, edits, clearing and route changes cancel obsolete work. Out-of-order or cancelled replies cannot replace the current results.",
    "A failed or unavailable worker uses a cooperative fallback that yields between indexing/scanning batches. Worker stalls are bounded; invalid versions, malformed replies and content failures are refused. A failed book never yields partial-library totals; failed preparation can retry.",
    "Search starts on demand and remains memory-only. Normal reading does not load every book or start a worker. Background and fallback modules are included in the verified offline reading pack."
  ],
